# Verify Email & Forgot Password Implementation

This plan outlines the steps to build the email-based authentication features using your existing Prisma schema (`verifyEmailToken`, `forgotPasswordToken`, etc.) and `nodemailer` for email delivery.

## Proposed Changes

We will build four new API endpoints and an email utility to handle the complete password reset and email verification lifecycles.

### 1. Dependencies
- Install `nodemailer` and `@types/nodemailer` to handle SMTP email sending.

### 2. Utilities
#### [NEW] `lib/email.ts`
- Create a reusable Nodemailer transport configuration.
- Add helper functions: `sendVerificationEmail(to, token)` and `sendPasswordResetEmail(to, token)`.
- It will read SMTP credentials from your `.env` file.

### 3. API Routes

#### [NEW] `app/api/auth/verify-email/send/route.ts`
- Generates a secure random 32-byte hex token.
- Updates the user's `verifyEmailToken` and `verifyEmailTokenExpiry` (e.g., 24 hours from now) in the database.
- Uses `lib/email.ts` to email a verification link to the user.

#### [NEW] `app/api/auth/verify-email/confirm/route.ts`
- Accepts the `token` from the URL.
- Looks up the user by token.
- Checks if the token has expired.
- If valid, updates `isEmailVerified` to `true` and nullifies the token fields.

#### [NEW] `app/api/auth/forgot-password/route.ts`
- Accepts an `email` address.
- If the user exists, generates a random hex token.
- Updates `forgotPasswordToken` and `forgotPasswordTokenExpiry` (e.g., 1 hour from now).
- Uses `lib/email.ts` to send the password reset link.

#### [NEW] `app/api/auth/reset-password/route.ts`
- Accepts the `token` and a `newPassword`.
- Looks up the user by token and checks expiration.
- Hashes the `newPassword` using `bcryptjs`.
- Updates the user's `passwordHash` and nullifies the token fields.

